From b047f0ea8f89d089e675778a78ef784e73a1e115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anirudh Acharya <anirudhra@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:17:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm: ifc6410: fix MSM IOMMU page table allocation

Backport ARM DMA mapping and MSM IOMMU fixes needed for APQ8064 display and Adreno initialization.

Use the MSM IOMMU device rather than the GPU/display client device for ARMv7 page-table allocation after releasing the legacy client mapping.

Validated on IFC6410:
- Debian boots to multi-user target
- MSM DRM binds Adreno A3xx and loads A300 PM4/PFP firmware
- EGL surfaceless and GBM both report Mesa Freedreno FD320
---
